{"session_id":"svc-1779863974693819472","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-27T06:39:35.876045942Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"haiku","sticky":{"key_present":true,"assignment":"not_applicable","bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"resolved_harness":"claude","harness_source":"auto_route","resolved_model":"haiku","work_dir":"/Users/erik/Projects/.ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-clone-fizeau-33a2ad0f-20260527T063922-35b63967","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead in an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the contract: every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, use a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, children once more; reject third-level splits with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path with child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Decomposition alone is success. Do not mix it with implementation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC to concrete evidence (test, file, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Run git/index mutations sequentially; do not use parallel tool calls for `git add`, `git commit`, or other staging/commit commands.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- If `lefthook run pre-commit` depends on staged files, rerun it after staging the exact commit set. A `no-staged-files` run is not acceptance evidence.\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- Current-bead lifecycle is orchestrator-owned. Do not run `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --claim`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --status \u0026lt;status\u0026gt;`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --unclaim`, or `ddx bead close \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;`. Step 0 still allows `ddx bead create`, `ddx bead dep add`, and `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path before exiting. No commit or rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The `no_changes_rationale.txt` file under the bead metadata `bundle` path must contain one of:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` are rejected.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;For orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Reports go under the bead metadata `bundle` path in `.ddx/executions/`. **Never write reports to `/tmp` or outside the repo**. Use a named in-repo path when given; otherwise write `\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md` there. Commit it with the code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other instruction files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-33a2ad0f\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eclaude-tui/gate: reconcile `claude --print` measurement section\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nPROBLEM: ADR-013\u0026#39;s economic premise requires the `--print mode measurements` section to show exactly three complete empirical runs. Even after individual captures are added, the section still needs an aggregate reconciliation proving the parent verification requirements across all runs.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ROOT CAUSE: docs/helix/02-design/billing-observation-claude-tui.md:1 uses the `--print mode measurements` placeholder as the source of truth, but no aggregate check confirms exactly three labeled runs, six snapshots, three outputs, timestamp coverage, refresh-delay compliance, and whole-window single-account attestation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX: Dependency ID: fizeau-a45dafe6. Governing artifact: ADR-013. Audit only the `--print mode measurements` section of docs/helix/02-design/billing-observation-claude-tui.md. Normalize labels to exactly `Run 1`, `Run 2`, and `Run 3`; remove accidental duplicate empty placeholders; verify each run has BEFORE and AFTER `/usage` snapshots, full turn output, wall-clock snapshot timestamps, completion timestamp, and proof that AFTER was captured at refresh-delay + safety margin, \u0026gt;=60s post-completion. Add or tighten a single-account attestation covering the full `--print` measurement window. Do not invent missing measurement data; if evidence is missing, mark the bead blocked and name the missing run evidence.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;NON-SCOPE: PTY+hooks measurements, delta computation, verdict determination, ADR-013 disposition, methodology authoring, new `claude --print` captures unless replacing explicitly missing or malformed evidence is operator-approved.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;AC:\u0026#xA;1) TestPrintModeExactlyThreeRuns: doc\u0026#39;s `--print mode measurements` section contains exactly three labeled runs: Run 1, Run 2, and Run 3.\u0026#xA;2) TestPrintModeSixSnapshots: the three runs contain exactly six `/usage` snapshot blocks, one BEFORE and one AFTER per run.\u0026#xA;3) TestPrintModeAllTurnOutputsPresent: each of the three runs has captured turn output.\u0026#xA;4) TestPrintModeAllSnapshotTimestampsPresent: every `/usage` snapshot has a wall-clock timestamp.\u0026#xA;5) TestPrintModeAllAfterRefreshDelaysVerified: every AFTER snapshot timestamp is \u0026gt;= that run\u0026#39;s completion-time + documented refresh-delay safety margin and \u0026gt;=60s post-completion.\u0026#xA;6) TestPrintModeWholeWindowSingleAccountAttested: the section attests no concurrent claude activity from the same account across the full `--print` measurement window.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;GATES: `go test ./...` passes; `lefthook run pre-commit` passes.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1) TestPrintModeExactlyThreeRuns\u0026#xA;2) TestPrintModeSixSnapshots\u0026#xA;3) TestPrintModeAllTurnOutputsPresent\u0026#xA;4) TestPrintModeAllSnapshotTimestampsPresent\u0026#xA;5) TestPrintModeAllAfterRefreshDelaysVerified\u0026#xA;6) TestPrintModeWholeWindowSingleAccountAttested\u0026#xA;Gates: `go test ./...`, `lefthook run pre-commit`.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003ehelix, phase:discover, kind:experiment, area:harness, harness:claude-tui, spec:ADR-013, gate:promotion\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-cc0dd5b2\" base-rev=\"fd4e907b33d8766fd973d5be01445b50d7b81430\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260527T063922-35b63967\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read them first. Ground decisions in repository state; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL":"/Users/erik/Projects/.ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-clone-fizeau-33a2ad0f-20260527T063922-35b63967/.ddx/executions/20260527T063922-35b63967/embedded/git-global.cfg","GIT_CONFIG_SYST